IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ky-ktap`
IMPORT `ky-ktap-seat`

-- KTAP -- worked cases from the applicant's seat. Expected values worked by hand from KRS 205.193, 205.200 and 921 KAR
-- 2:016 (eff. 2-16-2023) before the encoding was run, with the printed figures (cost-of-living factor 1) unless a case
-- says otherwise. Each assertion is a claim about the encoding on stated facts, not about the law.

§ `Cases`

§§ `The monthly payment`

-- Inputs: group size, cost-of-living factor, liquid assets, gross earnings, workers, dependent care disregard, in the
-- 50% months, deductions lost, unearned income, child support deducted, excluded unearned income.

-- A. A mother and two children with no income: the payment maximum, $524 (KRS 205.200(2); Section 9(4)(b)).
#ASSERT `How much KTAP would we get` 3 1 500 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 EQUALS `a monthly KTAP payment of` 524
-- B. The same family with $100 a month of unemployment benefit: countable 100; deficit 631 - 100 = 531; 55% = 292.05,
-- less than 524. (One dollar of income costs the family $231.95: NOTES.md finding 1.)
#ASSERT `How much KTAP would we get` 3 1 500 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE 100 0 0 EQUALS `a monthly KTAP payment of` 292.05
-- C. The mother earns $800: 800 - 175 = 625, within 631; 55% of 6 = 3.30.
#ASSERT `How much KTAP would we get` 3 1 500 800 1 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 EQUALS `a monthly KTAP payment of` 3.3
-- D. The same in one of the six months of the 50% disregard: 625 x 50% = 312.50; 55% of 318.50 = 175.175.
#ASSERT `How much KTAP would we get` 3 1 500 800 1 0 TRUE FALSE 0 0 0 EQUALS `a monthly KTAP payment of` 175.175
-- E. She earns $1,200: over the $1,169 gross income limit for 3.
#ASSERT `How much KTAP would we get` 3 1 500 1200 1 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 EQUALS `ineligible: gross income over the gross income limit (Section 4(1)(c))`
-- F. She earns $1,000: 825 countable is over the 631 standard of need.
#ASSERT `How much KTAP would we get` 3 1 500 1000 1 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 EQUALS `ineligible: countable income over the standard of need (Section 4(2)(b))`
-- G. Liquid assets of $12,000.
#ASSERT `How much KTAP would we get` 3 1 12000 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 EQUALS `ineligible: resources over $10,000 (921 KAR 2:016 Section 3(2))`
-- H. One eligible person with $481 of unearned income: within the standard of need, but 55% of 0 is 0.
#ASSERT `How much KTAP would we get` 1 1 0 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE 481 0 0 EQUALS `ineligible: the payment would be zero (Section 9(5))`
-- I. Two persons, no income, with a 1.05 cost-of-living factor: 450 x 1.05 = 472.50.
#ASSERT `How much KTAP would we get` 2 1.05 0 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 EQUALS `a monthly KTAP payment of` 472.5
-- J. Earnings of $600: 600 - 175 = 425; 55% of 206 = 113.30. With the deductions lost (a pay rise not reported in ten
-- days), the $600 counts in full: 55% of 31 = 17.05.
#ASSERT `How much KTAP would we get` 3 1 0 600 1 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 EQUALS `a monthly KTAP payment of` 113.3
#ASSERT `How much KTAP would we get` 3 1 0 600 1 0 FALSE TRUE 0 0 0 EQUALS `a monthly KTAP payment of` 17.05
-- K. $300 of child support, all assigned and forwarded to the cabinet: countable 0, but the family has income, so 55% of
-- 631 = 347.05, not the payment maximum.
#ASSERT `How much KTAP would we get` 3 1 0 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE 300 300 0 EQUALS `a monthly KTAP payment of` 347.05

§§ `The standards`

#ASSERT `What is our payment maximum` 7 1 EQUALS 964
#ASSERT `What is our payment maximum` 9 1 EQUALS 964
#ASSERT `What is our gross income limit` 4 1 EQUALS 1315
#ASSERT `Are our assets within the limit` 10000 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Are our assets within the limit` 10001 EQUALS FALSE

§§ `KRS 205.200(7), 205.193; 921 KAR 2:016 Section 5(4)(b)`

#ASSERT `Am I barred for refusing work` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I barred for refusing work` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I barred for refusing work` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `By when must I report the increase` (DATE_FROM_DMY 20 10 2026) EQUALS (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 10 2026)
#ASSERT `Most months stopped for EBT misuse` 1 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `Most months stopped for EBT misuse` 2 EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `Most months stopped for EBT misuse` 5 EQUALS 12

-- The duties, in days from the change in earnings.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `the Section 5(4)(b) report of an increase in earnings` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the recipient` `report the increase in earnings` 8)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the recipient, "the increase in earnings was not reported within ten days of the change ..." (reported on day 12)
#TRACE `the Section 5(4)(b) report of an increase in earnings` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the recipient` DOES `report the increase in earnings` AT 12
-- expect: BREACH BY the recipient, "cash withdrawn with the EBT card was used other than for goods and services necessary for the welfare of the family ..."
#TRACE `the 205.193(2) restriction on cash withdrawn` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the recipient` DOES `use cash withdrawn with the EBT card other than for goods and services necessary for the welfare of the family` AT 3
